## pengu
## Layer-2 wrapper over the 56 font and text functions of the `raylib` binding.
##
## This is the busiest family for the string boundary, and the header does not make the
## two ownership families obvious, so they were measured (see the family plan D2):
##
## - `text_upper`, `text_lower`, `text_pascal`, `text_snake`, `text_camel`, `text_subtext`,
##   `text_without_spaces`, `text_between`, `text_replace`, `text_replace_between`,
##   `text_insert`, `text_join`, `split_text` and `codepoint_to_text` return a **static
##   buffer that the next call to the same function overwrites**. The wrapper copies it into
##   an owned `string` and frees nothing.
## - `text_replace_alloc`, `text_replace_between_alloc` and `text_insert_alloc` return a
##   **fresh allocation**. The wrapper copies it and frees it with `MemFree`.
##
## Five methods live on `raylib.Font` (`draw`, `draw_pro`, `draw_codepoint`,
## `draw_codepoints`, `measure`); everything else is a module-level function.
##
## This is family `text` of `raylibx`; see `docs/wrappers/raylibx-text.md`.
##
## ## A headless process has no usable font
## Outside `InitWindow`, `GetFontDefault()` returns a `Font` with `glyphCount == 0` and a
## null glyph table, and measuring or querying a glyph on it **segfaults** (measured). Only
## the pure text and codepoint groups are asserted in CI; the font lifecycle, the glyph
## queries and the drawing entries are type-checked by `draw_api_probe` and not called.
##
## ## Memory
## Nothing is leaked and nothing is freed twice: the three `*_alloc` results and the
## `GenImageFontAtlas` rectangle array are `MemFree`d inside their wrappers, and
## `UnloadFontData`/`UnloadCodepoints` are called inside the wrappers that own those
## buffers. The caller always receives an owned PenguScript value.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## import raylib
## import raylibx_text
##
## weave main into int:
##     var parts as list of string is calling split_text with "a,b,c", 44
##     defer banish parts
##     var joined as string is calling text_join with (parts at 0 to (parts.length)), "-"
##     var shouty as string is calling text_upper with joined
##     return parts.length
## ```


import raylib
import std.ffi
import std.ward

enchanting raylib.Font:

    ## Draws text at a position using this font.
    ##
    ## ## Parameters
    ## - `text`: the text to draw.
    ## - `position`: the anchor point.
    ## - `font_size`: the font size in pixels.
    ## - `spacing`: the extra spacing between characters.
    ## - `tint`: the text colour.
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## Nothing; the text is drawn into the current frame.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## Requires an active drawing frame (`BeginDrawing`/`EndDrawing`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
    ## The font's `baseSize` is the size the glyphs were rasterised at; drawing at a different `font_size` scales the texture and may look soft.
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## calling font.draw with "hello", (with x is 10.0, y is 10.0), 20.0, 1.0, raylib.RAYWHITE
    ## ```

    weave draw with text as string, position as raylib.Vector2, font_size as f32, spacing as f32, tint as raylib.Color into void:
        let c_text as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with text
        calling raylib.DrawTextEx with (essence of self), c_text, position, font_size, spacing, tint

    ## Draws text with a rotation around an origin.
    ##
    ## ## Parameters
    ## - `text`: the text to draw.
    ## - `position`: the anchor point.
    ## - `origin`: the rotation pivot, relative to `position`.
    ## - `rotation`: the rotation in degrees.
    ## - `font_size`: the font size in pixels.
    ## - `spacing`: the extra spacing between characters.
    ## - `tint`: the text colour.
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## Nothing; the text is drawn into the current frame.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## Requires an active drawing frame (`BeginDrawing`/`EndDrawing`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## calling font.draw_pro with "hello", pos, (with x is 0.0, y is 0.0), 45.0, 20.0, 1.0, raylib.RAYWHITE
    ## ```

    weave draw_pro with text as string, position as raylib.Vector2, origin as raylib.Vector2, rotation as f32, font_size as f32, spacing as f32, tint as raylib.Color into void:
        let c_text as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with text
        calling raylib.DrawTextPro with (essence of self), c_text, position, origin, rotation, font_size, spacing, tint

    ## Draws a single character by its codepoint.
    ##
    ## ## Parameters
    ## - `codepoint`: the unicode codepoint to draw.
    ## - `position`: the anchor point.
    ## - `font_size`: the font size in pixels.
    ## - `tint`: the character colour.
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## Nothing; the character is drawn into the current frame.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## Requires an active drawing frame (`BeginDrawing`/`EndDrawing`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## calling font.draw_codepoint with 65, pos, 20.0, raylib.RAYWHITE
    ## ```

    weave draw_codepoint with codepoint as int, position as raylib.Vector2, font_size as f32, tint as raylib.Color into void:
        calling raylib.DrawTextCodepoint with (essence of self), codepoint, position, font_size, tint

    ## Draws a run of characters given as codepoints.
    ##
    ## ## Parameters
    ## - `codepoints`: the codepoints to draw, in order.
    ## - `position`: the anchor point.
    ## - `font_size`: the font size in pixels.
    ## - `spacing`: the extra spacing between characters.
    ## - `tint`: the text colour.
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## Nothing; the run is drawn into the current frame.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## Requires an active drawing frame (`BeginDrawing`/`EndDrawing`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
    ## An empty `codepoints` slice draws nothing and is not an error.
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## calling font.draw_codepoints with (points at 0 to 3), pos, 20.0, 1.0, raylib.RAYWHITE
    ## ```

    weave draw_codepoints with codepoints as slice of int, position as raylib.Vector2, font_size as f32, spacing as f32, tint as raylib.Color into void:
        if (codepoints.length) == 0:
            return
        let raw as ref to void is transmute (sigil of (codepoints at 0)) to (ref to void)
        calling raylib.DrawTextCodepoints with (essence of self), raw, (codepoints.length), position, font_size, spacing, tint

    ## Measures the size the text would occupy in this font.
    ##
    ## ## Parameters
    ## - `text`: the text to measure.
    ## - `font_size`: the font size in pixels.
    ## - `spacing`: the extra spacing between characters.
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## A `raylib.Vector2` with the width and height in pixels.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## **A headless process cannot call this**: it walks the font's glyph table, which is null before `InitWindow` (the family plan D16). With a real font loaded it is pure arithmetic and needs no drawing frame.
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## var size as raylib.Vector2 is calling font.measure with "hello", 20.0, 1.0
    ## ```

    weave measure with text as string, font_size as f32, spacing as f32 into raylib.Vector2:
        let c_text as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with text
        return calling raylib.MeasureTextEx with (essence of self), c_text, font_size, spacing

## Returns raylib's built-in default font.
##
## ## Returns
## The default `raylib.Font`.
##
## ## Notes
## **Outside `InitWindow` this font is unusable**: raylib has not loaded its glyph table yet, so `glyphCount` is `0` and measuring or querying a glyph on it crashes (measured). It is safe to *obtain*, not to *use*, without a window.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var font as raylib.Font is calling default_font
## ```

weave default_font into raylib.Font:
    return calling raylib.GetFontDefault

## Loads a font from a file.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `path`: the font file (`.ttf`/`.otf`, or a raylib `.fnt`).
##
## ## Returns
## `some` with a valid font, or `maybe none` when raylib could not load it.
##
## ## Notes
## The font is an external resource: release it with `unload_font` when done.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var font as maybe raylib.Font is calling load_font with "arial.ttf"
## ```

weave load_font with path as string into maybe raylib.Font:
    let c_path as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with path
    var font as raylib.Font is calling raylib.LoadFont with c_path
    if calling raylib.IsFontValid with font:
        return some font
    return maybe none

## Loads a font at a given size with an explicit codepoint set.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `path`: the font file.
## - `font_size`: the rasterisation size in pixels.
## - `codepoints`: the codepoints to bake, or an empty slice for raylib's default set.
##
## ## Returns
## `some` with a valid font, or `maybe none`.
##
## ## Notes
## An empty `codepoints` slice passes a null pointer, which is raylib's "use the default 95 ASCII characters" signal.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var font as maybe raylib.Font is calling load_font_ex with "arial.ttf", 32, (points at 0 to 0)
## ```

weave load_font_ex with path as string, font_size as int, codepoints as slice of int into maybe raylib.Font:
    let c_path as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with path
    var raw as ref to void is calling ffi.null_void
    if (codepoints.length) > 0:
        let raw as ref to void is transmute (sigil of (codepoints at 0)) to (ref to void)
    var font as raylib.Font is calling raylib.LoadFontEx with c_path, font_size, transmute raw to ref to frozen int, (codepoints.length)
    if calling raylib.IsFontValid with font:
        return some font
    return maybe none

## Builds a font from an image whose glyphs are separated by a key colour.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `image`: the source image, laid out as a grid of glyphs.
## - `key`: the background colour to treat as transparent.
## - `first_char`: the codepoint of the first glyph in the image.
##
## ## Returns
## `some` with a valid font, or `maybe none`.
##
## ## Notes
## The image is only read, not consumed: it stays the caller's to unload.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var font as maybe raylib.Font is calling load_font_from_image with img, raylib.MAGENTA, 32
## ```

weave load_font_from_image with image as raylib.Image, key as raylib.Color, first_char as int into maybe raylib.Font:
    var font as raylib.Font is calling raylib.LoadFontFromImage with image, key, first_char
    if calling raylib.IsFontValid with font:
        return some font
    return maybe none

## Loads a font from a byte buffer already in memory.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `file_type`: the file extension raylib should parse, for example `".ttf"`.
## - `data`: the font file contents.
## - `font_size`: the rasterisation size in pixels.
## - `codepoints`: the codepoints to bake, or an empty slice for the default set.
##
## ## Returns
## `some` with a valid font, or `maybe none` when `data` is empty or raylib fails.
##
## ## Notes
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var font as maybe raylib.Font is calling load_font_from_memory with ".ttf", blob, 32, (points at 0 to 0)
## ```

weave load_font_from_memory with file_type as string, data as slice of byte, font_size as int, codepoints as slice of int into maybe raylib.Font:
    let c_type as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with file_type
    if (data.length) == 0:
        return maybe none
    let raw as ref to frozen byte is transmute (sigil of (data at 0)) to ref to frozen byte
    var cps as ref to void is calling ffi.null_void
    if (codepoints.length) > 0:
        let cps as ref to void is transmute (sigil of (codepoints at 0)) to (ref to void)
    var font as raylib.Font is calling raylib.LoadFontFromMemory with c_type, raw, (data.length), font_size, transmute cps to ref to frozen int, (codepoints.length)
    if calling raylib.IsFontValid with font:
        return some font
    return maybe none

## Reports whether a font holds a usable glyph table.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `font`: the font to check.
##
## ## Returns
## `true` when raylib considers the font loaded.
##
## ## Notes
## This is the predicate behind every `load_font*` `maybe` in this family.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var ok as bool is calling is_font_valid with font
## ```

weave is_font_valid with font as raylib.Font into bool:
    return calling raylib.IsFontValid with font

## Releases a font loaded from a file or from memory.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `font`: the font to release.
##
## ## Returns
## Nothing.
##
## ## Notes
## Do **not** call this on `default_font`: that one belongs to raylib.
## After unloading, the `Font` value must not be used again.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling unload_font with font
## ```

weave unload_font with font as raylib.Font into void:
    calling raylib.UnloadFont with font

## Writes a font as a C source file.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `font`: the font to export.
## - `path`: the `.c`/`.h` destination.
##
## ## Returns
## `true` when raylib reports success, `false` otherwise.
##
## ## Notes
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var ok as bool is calling export_font_as_code with font, "font.c"
## ```

weave export_font_as_code with font as raylib.Font, path as string into bool:
    let c_path as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with path
    return calling raylib.ExportFontAsCode with font, c_path

## Returns the index of a codepoint inside a font's glyph table.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `font`: the font to query.
## - `codepoint`: the unicode codepoint.
##
## ## Returns
## The glyph index, falling back to the index of `'?'` when the codepoint is missing.
##
## ## Notes
## **Window-bound**: it walks the glyph table, which is null before `InitWindow` (measured: it segfaults).
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var idx as int is calling font_glyph_index with font, 65
## ```

weave font_glyph_index with font as raylib.Font, codepoint as int into int:
    return calling raylib.GetGlyphIndex with font, codepoint

## Returns the glyph record for a codepoint.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `font`: the font to query.
## - `codepoint`: the unicode codepoint.
##
## ## Returns
## A `raylib.GlyphInfo`; missing codepoints fall back to `'?'`.
##
## ## Notes
## **Window-bound**, same reason as `font_glyph_index`.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var info as raylib.GlyphInfo is calling font_glyph_info with font, 65
## ```

weave font_glyph_info with font as raylib.Font, codepoint as int into raylib.GlyphInfo:
    return calling raylib.GetGlyphInfo with font, codepoint

## Returns the atlas rectangle a glyph occupies.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `font`: the font to query.
## - `codepoint`: the unicode codepoint.
##
## ## Returns
## The glyph's `raylib.Rectangle` inside the font atlas texture.
##
## ## Notes
## **Window-bound**, same reason as `font_glyph_index`.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var rec as raylib.Rectangle is calling font_glyph_atlas_rec with font, 65
## ```

weave font_glyph_atlas_rec with font as raylib.Font, codepoint as int into raylib.Rectangle:
    return calling raylib.GetGlyphAtlasRec with font, codepoint

## Decodes the glyph data of a font file held in memory.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `data`: the font file contents.
## - `font_size`: the rasterisation size in pixels.
## - `codepoints`: the codepoints to decode, or an empty slice for the default set.
## - `kind`: the data type to request; `0` is the default 8-bit antialiased format.
##
## ## Returns
## An owned list of `raylib.GlyphInfo`; empty when `data` is empty or raylib fails.
##
## ## Notes
## This is the low-level step behind `load_font_ex`. The raylib buffer is released with `UnloadFontData` inside the wrapper, so the returned list is entirely PenguScript-owned.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var glyphs as list of raylib.GlyphInfo is calling load_font_data with blob, 32, (points at 0 to 0), 0
## ```

weave load_font_data with data as slice of byte, font_size as int, codepoints as slice of int, kind as int into list of raylib.GlyphInfo:
    if (data.length) == 0:
        return list of raylib.GlyphInfo
    let raw as ref to frozen byte is transmute (sigil of (data at 0)) to ref to frozen byte
    var cps as ref to void is calling ffi.null_void
    if (codepoints.length) > 0:
        let cps as ref to void is transmute (sigil of (codepoints at 0)) to (ref to void)
    var n as int is 0
    var glyphs as ref to raylib.GlyphInfo is calling raylib.LoadFontData with raw, (data.length), font_size, transmute cps to ref to frozen int, (codepoints.length), kind, sigil of n
    if calling ffi.is_null with (transmute glyphs to ref to void):
        return list of raylib.GlyphInfo
    let as_void as ref to void is transmute glyphs to ref to void
    var owned as list of raylib.GlyphInfo is calling ffi.list_from_ptr of raylib.GlyphInfo with as_void, n
    calling raylib.UnloadFontData with glyphs, n
    return owned

## Packs glyphs into a font atlas image.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `glyphs`: the glyph records, typically from `load_font_data`.
## - `font_size`: the font size in pixels.
## - `padding`: the padding between glyphs in the atlas.
## - `pack_method`: the packing algorithm; `0` is the default.
##
## ## Returns
## A new `raylib.Image` holding the atlas.
##
## ## Notes
## raylib allocates an array of atlas rectangles and hands it back through an out-parameter; the wrapper **frees it with `MemFree`** and returns only the image, so that array is not part of the public surface (family plan D11).
## An empty `glyphs` slice returns a 1x1 blank image instead of calling into raylib, because the C function would read a null glyph pointer.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var atlas as raylib.Image is calling font_atlas_image with (glyphs at 0 to 3), 32, 1, 0
## ```

weave font_atlas_image with glyphs as slice of raylib.GlyphInfo, font_size as int, padding as int, pack_method as int into raylib.Image:
    if (glyphs.length) == 0:
        return calling raylib.GenImageColor with 1, 1, raylib.BLANK
    let raw as ref to void is transmute (sigil of (glyphs at 0)) to (ref to void)
    var recs as ref to void is calling ffi.null_void
    var atlas as raylib.Image is calling raylib.GenImageFontAtlas with raw, transmute (sigil of recs) to (ref to void), (glyphs.length), font_size, padding, pack_method
    if calling ffi.is_valid with recs:
        calling raylib.MemFree with recs
    return atlas

## Draws the current frame rate using the default font.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `x`, `y`: the top-left corner of the readout.
##
## ## Returns
## Nothing; the readout is drawn into the current frame.
##
## ## Notes
## Requires an active drawing frame (`BeginDrawing`/`EndDrawing`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
## raylib owns the string it formats internally; nothing is allocated here.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling draw_fps with 10, 10
## ```

weave draw_fps with x as int, y as int into void:
    calling raylib.DrawFPS with x, y

## Draws text using raylib's default font.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `text`: the text to draw.
## - `x`, `y`: the top-left corner.
## - `font_size`: the font size in pixels.
## - `color`: the text colour.
##
## ## Returns
## Nothing; the text is drawn into the current frame.
##
## ## Notes
## Requires an active drawing frame (`BeginDrawing`/`EndDrawing`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
## This is the default-font variant of `Font.draw`: no font argument, no letter spacing.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling draw_text with "hello", 10, 10, 20, raylib.RAYWHITE
## ```

weave draw_text with text as string, x as int, y as int, font_size as int, color as raylib.Color into void:
    let c_text as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with text
    calling raylib.DrawText with c_text, x, y, font_size, color

## Measures the width of text in the default font.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `text`: the text to measure.
## - `font_size`: the font size in pixels.
##
## ## Returns
## The width in pixels, or `0` when the text is empty.
##
## ## Notes
## This returns a width only; `Font.measure` returns width and height for an explicit font.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var w as int is calling measure_text with "hello", 20
## ```

weave measure_text with text as string, font_size as int into int:
    let c_text as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with text
    return calling raylib.MeasureText with c_text, font_size

## Converts text to upper case.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `text`: the text to transform.
##
## ## Returns
## The upper-case text.
##
## ## Notes
## raylib returns a **static buffer** that the next call to this same function overwrites; the wrapper copies it immediately, so the returned `string` is safe to keep.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var s as string is calling text_upper with "hello"
## ```

weave text_upper with text as string into string:
    let c_text as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with text
    return calling ffi.string_from_cstr with (transmute (calling raylib.TextToUpper with c_text) to ref to char)

## Converts text to lower case.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `text`: the text to transform.
##
## ## Returns
## The lower-case text.
##
## ## Notes
## raylib returns a **static buffer** that the next call to this same function overwrites; the wrapper copies it immediately, so the returned `string` is safe to keep.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var s as string is calling text_lower with "HELLO"
## ```

weave text_lower with text as string into string:
    let c_text as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with text
    return calling ffi.string_from_cstr with (transmute (calling raylib.TextToLower with c_text) to ref to char)

## Converts text to Pascal case notation.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `text`: the text to transform.
##
## ## Returns
## The Pascal-case text.
##
## ## Notes
## raylib returns a **static buffer** that the next call to this same function overwrites; the wrapper copies it immediately, so the returned `string` is safe to keep.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var s as string is calling text_pascal with "hello world"
## ```

weave text_pascal with text as string into string:
    let c_text as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with text
    return calling ffi.string_from_cstr with (transmute (calling raylib.TextToPascal with c_text) to ref to char)

