## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var s as string is calling codepoint_to_text with 65
## ```

weave codepoint_to_text with codepoint as int into string:
    var n as int is 0
    return calling ffi.string_from_cstr with (transmute (calling raylib.CodepointToUTF8 with codepoint, sigil of n) to ref to char)

## Decodes a UTF-8 string into its codepoints.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `text`: the text to decode.
##
## ## Returns
## An owned list with one entry per codepoint; empty when raylib fails.
##
## ## Notes
## raylib allocates the array, so the wrapper copies it and releases it with `UnloadCodepoints` before returning.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var cps as list of int is calling codepoints_from_text with "hi"
## ```

weave codepoints_from_text with text as string into list of int:
    let c_text as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with text
    var n as int is 0
    var cps as ref to int is calling raylib.LoadCodepoints with c_text, sigil of n
    if calling ffi.is_null with (transmute cps to ref to void):
        return list of int
    let as_void as ref to void is transmute cps to ref to void
    var owned as list of int is calling ffi.list_of_int_from_ptr with as_void, n
    calling raylib.UnloadCodepoints with cps
    return owned

## Encodes a list of codepoints as a UTF-8 string.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `codepoints`: the codepoints to encode.
##
## ## Returns
## `some` with the encoded text, or `maybe none` for an empty slice or a raylib failure.
##
## ## Notes
## **An empty slice and a failure are both `maybe none`**: raylib returns a null pointer for a zero length, so the wrapper cannot tell them apart (measured). Documented rather than hidden.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation by the wrapper; any raylib buffer is copied and released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var text as maybe string is calling text_from_codepoints with (points at 0 to 2)
## ```

weave text_from_codepoints with codepoints as slice of int into maybe string:
    if (codepoints.length) == 0:
        return maybe none
    let raw as ref to frozen int is transmute (sigil of (codepoints at 0)) to (ref to frozen int)
    var text as ref to char is calling raylib.LoadUTF8 with raw, (codepoints.length)
    if calling ffi.is_null with (transmute text to ref to void):
        return maybe none
    var owned as string is calling ffi.string_from_cstr with text
    calling raylib.UnloadUTF8 with text
    return some owned

## Sets the vertical spacing between lines of text.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `spacing`: the line spacing in pixels.
##
## ## Returns
